  "description": "First entry with a commarea present and no user pre-selected: the NOT CDEMO-PGM-REENTER arm at app/cbl/COUSR02C.cbl:95-105 with the CDEMO-CU02-USR-SELECTED test at :99-100 FALSE. The program sets CDEMO-PGM-REENTER, clears the output map with MOVE LOW-VALUES TO COUSR2AO, positions the cursor by moving -1 into USRIDINL, skips PROCESS-ENTER-KEY entirely and sends the empty screen once. No RECEIVE happens on this path, which is why mapFields is empty - a case that declared received fields here would be describing an input the program never took. ERRMSGO is 78 spaces because WS-MESSAGE was set to SPACES at :87 and never written to, and no attribute is pinned because no arm on this path moves a colour into ERRMSGC.\n\nThe five payload items are LOW-VALUES rather than spaces, and the distinction is behavioural. The MOVE LOW-VALUES TO COUSR2AO at :97 clears the whole output map to X'00', and the MOVEs that would put SPACES in those items - at :158-161 - live inside PROCESS-ENTER-KEY, which this path does not perform. BMS does not transmit a field whose data is X'00', so a screen cleared to LOW-VALUES and one cleared to spaces do not look the same at the terminal.",
